# Both tsconfigs declare `composite: true`, which makes tsc write an incremental build-info file
# beside them. The npm scripts pass `--composite false` so none exists today, but any editor or
# plain `tsc -b` produces one, and it is a build artifact either way.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor and OS droppings. .vscode/ is deliberately NOT here — its three files are checked in on
# purpose (debug launch configuration and the formatter choice).
.vs/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Per-machine agent configuration: absolute paths with the account name in them. This rule used
# to live only in a personal global ignore file, which protects one machine and no clone.
.claude/settings.local.json

# A skill-management CLI installs an unrelated marketing/design skill library here, outside this
# project's control. Ignore everything it adds and allowlist only what this project actually owns
# — a new marketing skill the tool installs later is ignored automatically, not swept in by a
# careless `git add -A`.
#
# .agents/skills/ is that CLI's install root and is ignored WHOLE. It used to allowlist the two
# agentation skills, which put a byte-identical second copy of each in the repository: git does
# not store a junction, it stores the files it finds, so a clone got two real directories that
# could drift apart with nothing to notice. `.claude/skills/` is the copy that is kept, because
# that is the path skills are actually discovered from — the CLI can restore its own tree from
# skills-lock.json, which records the source and hash of both.
.agents/

.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/agentation/
!.claude/skills/agentation-self-driving/
!.claude/skills/security-gates/
!.claude/skills/map-internals/
